BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:friends_of_trees_green_space
X-SOURCE:Friends Of Trees Green Space
DTSTART:20260424T154500Z
DTEND:20260424T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260425T021240Z
UID:6a9vt0pc7e0pbsrtbkejg1d8e6@google.com
CREATED:20260123T232035Z
DESCRIPTION:=======<br><br>Due to popular community support\, this event is
  <b><u>full and closed</u></b>. Thank you for your interest -- we hope to w
 ork with you in the future!<br><br>=======<br><br>Celebrate Earth Week by c
 aring for native trees and shrubs at this rare weekday event! <u>Note: ther
 e will be no tree-planting at this event\, and this can be physically-deman
 ding work</u> (great for folks looking for a work out!).  Our stewardship e
 vents help to ensure the highest level of plant survival through the PNW dr
 y summer months ahead.<p><b>Please arrive by 8:45am</b> to find our tent an
 d sign-in\, stewardship activities start promptly at 9:00am. We provide glo
 ves\, tools\, and guidance. All you need to do is show up dressed for the w
 eather and wearing sturdy shoes or boots (no sandals of any kind\, please!)
  and be ready to have fun!</p><p><b>Under age 18?</b> We request that youth
  15 and under volunteer with a parent/guardian.  Youth 16 and older can vol
 unteer on their own and will need to hand us a <b><a href="https://friendso
 ftrees.org/youthwaiver" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>youth
  waiver form</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a></b> signed by thei
 r parent/guardian.</p><p><b>Questions?  </b>Pl<u></u>ease check out our <a 
 href="https://friendsoftrees.org/volunteer-faq/" target="_blank"><u><u><u><
 u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>Volunteer FAQ webpage</u></b></u></u></u></
 u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>.  Our team is also happy to assist! 
 <a href="mailto:Volunteer@friendsoftrees.org" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><
 u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>volunteer@fr<u></u>iendsoftrees.or<u></u>g</u>
 </b></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a> / 503-595-0213 We 
 look forward to working together soon!</p><hr /><p>This event is in partner
 ship with City of Tualatin.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260417T204311Z
LOCATION:Tualatin Community Park\, 8515 SW Tualatin Rd\, Tualatin\, OR 9706
 2\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FULL - Tualatin Community Park Stewardship event (Tualatin\, OR)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
