X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lewis Clark": "https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/372691-ethical-considerations-in-psychedelic-assisted-psycho"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lewis_clark
X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
SUMMARY:Ethical Considerations in Psychedelic-Assisted Psychotherapy (In-P
 erson)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T100000
DTSTAMP:20251106T114252Z
UID:20260425T160000Z-372691@www.lclark.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T090000
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/91/width/80/height/80/crop/1/
 src_region/0,0,2133,3200/105597_pexels-igor-meghega-315695093-14489914.rev
 .1727901963.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This course offers an overview of the integration aspect of ps
 ychedelic-assisted therapy\, and examines ethical considerations that can 
 impact the overall and long-term experience of clients receiving treatment
 .  We will focus on integration as an intentional process of bringing awar
 eness to the impact of the psychedelic experience and applying it to one's
  life in ways that can be transformative.  Ethical issues\, harm reduction
  interventions in psychedelic-assisted therapy practices\, and anthropocen
 tric and biocentric perspectives on working with psychedelic medicines in 
 therapy will be discussed.Following the completion of this course\, partic
 ipants should have a better understanding of:How to apply tools to concept
 ualize and facilitate integration practices.  Affirmative ethics and harm 
 reduction frameworks\, and how they apply to psychedelic-assisted psychoth
 erapy.  Psychedelic-assisted psychotherapy from a biocentric perspective\,
  which focuses on the relationship between humans\, plant medicines\, psyc
 hedelic medicines\, and psychotherapy.  Integrating the diversity\, equity
 \, and inclusion dimensions of everyday life and clinical work into psyche
 delic therapy.  Course Details &amp\; RegistrationDates and Times: Saturda
 y-Sunday\, April 25-26\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-5:30 p.m.Location: Lewis &amp\; Cla
 rk Graduate School\, Portland\, OregonInstructors: Elizabeth Hoke\, LMFT\;
  and Veronica Vargas\, LPCGraduate-level Continuing Education credit: CECP
 -866-01\, 1 semester hour\, $375We are committed to making our events acce
 ssible to all needs and abilities. If you have a disability that may impac
 t your academic performance\, you may request accommodations by meeting wi
 th the Office of Student Accessibility staff and submitting documentation 
 on the Office of Student Accessibility website (/offices/student-accessibi
 lity/). Please be aware that the process for evaluation and implementation
  of accommodations could take 2-3 weeks\, so please be in touch with the O
 SA as soon as possible. Email access@lclark.edu (mailto:access@lclark.edu)
  with any additional questions or concerns.About the Instructors Elizabeth
  Hoke\, MFT is the Clinical Director of Liberation Institute in Portland w
 here she supervises and provides psychoeducational trainings and workshops
 . She specializes in working with addiction recovery and ADHD\, using a mi
 x of theoretical tools rooted in somatic psychology and biocentric philoso
 phies. Elizabeth co-facilitates ketamine-assisted psychotherapy sessions a
 t Rainfall Medicine and co-leads addiction recovery support groups at Port
 land Psychedelic Society and the Rhizome. She has completed the 100-hour M
 DMA Therapy Training program through the Multidisciplinary Association for
  Psychedelic Studies. Elizabeth also co-created the Entheogen Assisted Psy
 chotherapy and Integration Training Series for licensed professionals at L
 ewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School Center for Community Engagement in 2021.
  Veronica Vargas\, MA\, LPC journeys alongside folks in their path towards
  healing\, harmony\, and contentment. She finds beauty in witnessing the u
 nfolding of human potential\, and cultivation of meaning. Her formal train
 ing is in counseling psychology with an emphasis in depth-psychotherapy. D
 epth-psychotherapy can be defined as a holistic approach that examines all
  aspects of a person's life\, including dreams\, art\, fantasies\, philoso
 phies\, and conscious thoughts. She was heavily influenced by the work of 
 Swiss psychiatrist\, Carl Gustav Jung. In her work as a licensed psychothe
 rapist she assesses the whole person or family system by looking at relati
 onal and cultural systems\; spirituality\; personal and intergenerational 
 trauma\; systems of oppression\; personal values and how they are or aren'
 t reflected authentically in the person's life. She has a private practice
  in Portland\, Oregon where she offers psychotherapy\, dream work\, and ps
 ychedelic integration therapy. .  &#160\;New workshops and trainings are a
 dded to our calendar regularly. For the latest on professional development
  related to your specific interests\, sign up for our mailing list! (https
 ://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260420T180336Z
LOCATION:Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School\, TBA
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/372691-ethical-considera
 tions-in-psychedelic-assisted-psycho
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="line-height: 1.6\;">  This course o
 ffers an overview of the integration aspect of psychedelic-assisted therap
 y\, and examines ethical considerations that can impact the overall and lo
 ng-term experience of clients receiving treatment.</p><p style="line-heigh
 t: 1.6\;">  We will focus on integration as an intentional process of brin
 ging awareness to the impact of the psychedelic experience and applying it
  to one's life in ways that can be transformative.</p><p style="line-heigh
 t: 1.6\;">  Ethical issues\, harm reduction interventions in psychedelic-a
 ssisted therapy practices\, and anthropocentric and biocentric perspective
 s on working with psychedelic medicines in therapy will be discussed.</p><
 p style="line-height: 1.6\;"><strong>Following the completion of this cour
 se\, participants should have a better understanding of:</strong></p><ul><
 li style="line-height: 1.6\;">How to apply tools to conceptualize and faci
