BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:friends_of_trees_green_space
X-SOURCE:Friends Of Trees Green Space
DTSTART:20260425T164500Z
DTEND:20260425T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260425T021240Z
UID:3lnsv1bheagsc4i8hrk3lnp4h8@google.com
CREATED:20260123T232520Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><strong><b>====</b></strong></p><p><b style="font-weight: bo
 ld\;">Due to popular interest\, this event is <u>full and closed.</u> </b>W
 e hope to work with you at another of our April events and/or next planting
  season (which starts in Oct!).</p><p><strong><b>====</b></strong></p><p><s
 trong><b>Celebrate Earth Week with the </b></strong><a href="https://friend
 softrees.org/blog/greening-wilkes/" target="_blank"><u><strong><b>Greening 
 Wilkes</b></strong></u></a><strong><b> collective by mulching hundreds of n
 ative pollinator-friendly species at Wilkes Creek Headwaters! </b></strong>
 We may also take out some weedy introduced plants\, if time allows. <u>Note
 </u>: there will be no tree-planting at this event\, and this can be physic
 ally-demanding work (great for folks looking for a work out!). Our stewards
 hip events help to ensure the highest level of plant survival through the P
 NW dry summer months ahead. <b>This event will include bird walks led by th
 e Bird Alliance of Oregon\, and will end by 12pm so that people can join th
 e Greening Wilkes celebration from 12-1:30 at nearby Wilkes Park.</b></p><p
 >The celebration will involve lunch\, tabling and games from the Greening W
 ilkes partners- Portland Parks and Recreation\, Columbia Slough Watershed C
 ouncil\, Verde\, and The Bird Alliance of Oregon- as well as a native plant
  giveaway hosted by Friends of Trees! (Registration is not required to join
  the celebration\, but it is to participate in the stewardship event.) </p>
 <p><b>Please arrive by 9:45am</b> to find our tent and sign-in\, stewardshi
 p activities start promptly at 10:00am. We provide gloves\, tools\, and gui
 dance. All you need to do is show up dressed for the weather and wearing st
 urdy shoes or boots (no sandals of any kind\, please!) and be ready to have
  fun!</p><p><b>Under age 18?</b> We request that youth 15 and under volunte
 er with a parent/guardian.  Youth 16 and older can volunteer on their own a
 nd will need to hand us a <b><a href="https://friendsoftrees.org/youthwaive
 r" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>youth waiver form</u></
 u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a></b> signed by their parent/guard
 ian.</p><p><b>Questions?  </b>Pl<u></u>ease check out our <a href="https://
 friendsoftrees.org/volunteer-faq/" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>
 <u><u><u><u><u><b><u>Volunteer FAQ webpage</u></b></u></u></u></u></u></u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>.  Our team is also happy to assist! <a href
 ="mailto:Volunteer@friendsoftrees.org" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u
 ><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>volunteer@fr<u></u>iendsoftrees.or<u></u>g</u></b>
 </u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a> / 503-595-0213 We 
 look forward to working together soon!</p><hr /><p>This event is in partner
 ship with Portland Parks &amp\; Recreation and Portland OIC.</p><p>Funding 
 for this event is provided by the U.S. Department of Agriculture\, Forest S
 ervice.  This institution is an equal opportunity provider.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260415T182544Z
LOCATION:15401 NE Fremont St\, Portland\, OR 97230\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FULL - Wilkes Creek Headwaters Stewardship event (NE Portland\, OR)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
