X-SOURCE-ID:crystal_ballroom
X-SOURCE:Crystal Ballroom
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T100000
DTSTAMP:20260424T191224
CREATED:20260401T160135Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260401T160140Z
UID:10001073-1777197600-1777197600@www.crystalballroompdx.com
SUMMARY:Crystal Ballroom History & Art Tour
DESCRIPTION:Tour will meet outside the Box Office  \nJoin us as we explore the rich history of the Crystal Ballroom\, including police raids\, visits by silent screen idols and Beat poets\, psychedelic light shows\, R&B and rock legends\, dancing throughout the decades and narrow escapes from ruin.  \nThis tour may require standing for long periods of time and is mostly accessible via elevator. One stop on the tour\, the balcony\, can be seen but not accessed\, except by stairs.  \nPassport holders: This tour is eligible for the Crystal Ballroom and Lola’s Room location stamps and the Attend a History Sponsored Event experience stamp.
URL:https://www.crystalballroompdx.com/events/275938-crystal-ballroom-history-art-tour/
CATEGORIES:April
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.crystalballroompdx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/CrystalBallroomTours25-ACh39k.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Literary Arts": "https://literary-arts.org/event/bring-your-story-to-the-stage/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:literary_arts
X-SOURCE:Literary Arts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T143000
DTSTAMP:20260424T191201
CREATED:20260202T210700Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260416T174351Z
UID:10005631-1777197600-1777213800@literary-arts.org
SUMMARY:Bring Your Story to the Stage
DESCRIPTION:This class is for anyone ready to take a personal 5-minute story and actively shape it for an audience. You’ll work hands-on with one story. Drafting\, refining\, and testing it aloud. We’ll focus on structure\, pacing\, and point of view\, helping you find the spine of the story and decide what belongs in this particular version of the story and what doesn’t. You’ll practice starting strong\, building momentum\, and landing the story with intention. \nTaught by BACKFENCE Storytelling producers and hosts Frayn Masters and Ash Allen\, this class is ideal if you’ve taken Small Stories\, Big Meaning or already have a personal story you’re curious to bring forward—whether for a stage\, or simply to hear it land out loud. \nRather than “performing\,” this class emphasizes shaping a vulnerable narrative. You’ll receive demonstrations and feedback on mic use\, voice\, presence\, and timing in a supportive room\, with clear guidance.  \nBy the end of the workshop\, you’ll have:\n•	A shaped draft you can continue developing\n•	Practical tools for revising and rehearsing\n•	Greater confidence telling a personal story aloud\n•	A clearer sense of how you want to show up onstage \nYou set the pace. Participation is encouraged but never forced. The goal is clarity\, connection\, and momentum—not polish or performance. \nstrong>Access Program\nWe want our classes and seminars to be accessible to everyone\, regardless of income and background. We understand that our tuition structure can present obstacles for some people. Our Access Program offers writing class and seminar tuitions at a reduced rate. Most classes have at least one access spot available. \nPlease apply here for access rate tuition. Contact Susan Moore at susan@literary-arts.org if you have questions. \nLiaison position\nEvery in-person class and seminar at Literary Arts has one liaison position. Liaisons perform specific duties for each class meeting. If you are a liaison for a class or seminar\, the full amount of your tuition is covered by Literary Arts. \nApply here for the liaison position.
URL:https://literary-arts.org/event/bring-your-story-to-the-stage/
LOCATION:Literary Arts
CATEGORIES:Writing Classes,In-person,Storytelling
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://literary-arts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/template.jpeg
GEO:45.5213897;-122.6810304
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Portland Art Museum": "https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/heart-of-portland-miller-free-day/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:portland_art_museum
X-SOURCE:Portland Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260426T170000
DTSTAMP:20260424T191159
CREATED:20260319T182134Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260424T164806Z
UID:10001447-1777197600-1777222800@portlandartmuseum.org
SUMMARY:The 2026 HeART of Portland: K-12 Arts Showcase + Miller Family Free Day
DESCRIPTION:Overview\n\n\n\nWelcome to the HeART of Portland: K-12 Arts Showcase + Miller Family Free Day! Enjoy free admission all day in celebration of youth arts and the community partnership between the Museum and city schools. Make art\, see student performances\, and visit the HeART of Portland K-12 Visual Art Exhibition in the new Silver Family Youth and Community Gallery. Explore PAM’s new Rothko Pavilion and the exhibition David Hockney: Works from the Collection of Jordan D. Schnitzer and His Family Foundation which inspired the HeART of Portland collaborative art project.  \n\n\n\nFree tickets can be reserved online one week in advance and are also available at the door. \n\n\n\nSchedule\n\n\n\n11 am – 3 pmARTMAKING: Windows of Our Future Lana and Chris Finley Studio\, Level 0 Create colorful artwork inspired by the art of David Hockney and the architecture of PAM’s new Mark Rothko Pavilion. Facilitated by Portland Public Schools visual art teachers. \n\n\n\nSHORT FILMS BY STUDENTSStevens Room\, Level 0 See short films by Franklin and Roosevelt High School students. \n\n\n\n12 – 3 pmLook With MeSlow-looking conversations\, focused on one artwork at a time\, facilitated by PAM volunteer guides. Starting every half hour. Look for signs showing specific gallery locations. \n\n\n\n1 pm – 2 pm STUDENT PERFORMANCESMark Rothko Pavilion\, 3rd Floor OverlookEnjoy music and dance performances by Portland students of all ages. \n\n\n\n\nOliver Middle School Jazz Band \n\n\n\nRussell Elementary Rocket Choir\n\n\n\nJefferson Dancers\n\n\n\nThe Riverdale Ukulele Ensemble\n\n\n\n\nThank you\, Portlanders\, for the Arts Access Fund! The Arts Access Fund provides for elementary arts teachers in the six school districts serving Portland and for expanded access to the arts for all Portlanders. At this free day celebration\, we are thrilled to present student performances from four districts served by the Fund: Centennial\, Parkrose\, Portland Public Schools\, and Riverdale. \n\n\n\nMiller Family Free Days are generously supported by Sharon L. Miller and Family. Additional funding is provided by The Lamb Baldwin Foundation. \n\n\n\nRelated events\n\n\n\n\n\n			\n			\n							\n		\n		\n		\n		\n			\n							\n											Free & discounted\n						 x 											Lectures & talks\n															\n						\n							\n											\n												Look With Me												\n									\n						\n							\n										\n														\n								General accessibility							\n						\n										\n					\n		\n						\n			\n																	Apr 26\, 2026 \n			\n						\n							\n										1219 SW Park Ave \n				\n						\n					\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n			\n							\n		\n		\n		\n		\n			\n							\n											Exhibitions\n															\n						\n							\n											\n												2026 HeART of Portland: A Portland Public Schools K-12 Arts Showcase Visual Art Exhibition												\n									\n						\n					\n		\n						\n			\n																	Apr 15\, 2026 – Sep 20\, 2026 \n			\n						\n							\n										1219 SW Park Ave \n				\n						\n					\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n			\n							\n		\n		\n		\n		\n			\n							\n											Free & discounted\n						 x 											Partner events\n															\n						\n							\n											\n												2026 HeART of Portland: A Portland Public Schools K-12 Arts Showcase Opening Celebration												\n									\n						\n							\n										\n														\n								General accessibility							\n						\n										\n					\n		\n						\n			\n																	Apr 15\, 2026 \n			\n						\n							\n										1119 SW Park Ave
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/heart-of-portland-miller-free-day/
LOCATION:Portland Art Museum\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
CATEGORIES:Free & discounted
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://portlandartmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230423_MIller-Family-Free-Day-April-2023_0105-Unprocessed-JPEG-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
