DESCRIPTION:AI as Collaborator Workshop Part 1: The Creative SparkDuration
 : 1 HourLocation: Google Meet (Register (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e
 /1FAIpQLSd9ZO3fZCVD6c-Bmne4iMRUXyoVINidkRWNAjXjAsGhvBD5Xw/viewform?usp=hea
 der) for calendar invite)Description:  Move beyond using AI as just a "ven
 ding machine" (input -&gt\; output) and learn to use it as a collaborative
  thought partner. In the first session of our two-part series\, we will fo
 cus on Divergent Thinking—using AI to overcome writer's block\, generate
  creative ideas\, and expand your strategic thinking.What we will cover:Th
 e Mindset Shift: Moving from "Directive" to "Collaborative."    The Coach 
 Persona: How to get AI to help you outline and strategize.    The Muse Per
 sona: Generating volume\, variety\, and creative angles.    Live Demos: Br
 ing your laptop! We will be running live experiments.      AI as Collabora
 tor Workshop Part 2: The Critical LensDuration: 1 HourLocation: Google Mee
 tDescription: In Part 2\, we learn how to refine our ideas. This session f
 ocuses on Convergent Thinking—using AI to stress-test your logic\, polis
 h your tone\, and simulate audience reactions before you hit "send."What w
 e will cover:The Editor Persona: rewriting for tone\, clarity\, and impact
 .    The Devil's Advocate: Using AI to find holes in your logic and risks 
 in your plan.    The Virtual Focus Group: Simulating stakeholders (student
 s\, admin\, skeptics) to prep for difficult questions.    Pre-work: Please
  bring one "Ugly Draft" (an email\, policy\, or proposal that is unfinishe
 d or rough). We will use the tools to polish it live during the session.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260204T024048Z
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/382502-ai-as-collaborato
 r
