URL:https://anandaportland.org/events/devotion-yoga-in-daily-life-free-cla
 ss/
SUMMARY:Devotion:  Yoga in Daily Life FREE class
DESCRIPTION:\n“A single spark may start a forest fire. The smallest step 
 toward God can be a beginning in the process of soul-awakening. The Bhagav
 ad Gita says\, “To him who offers Me even a flower or a leaf with devo
 tion\, I Myself come and receive his offering.” The smallest expression 
 of pure love can be the spark that ignites a fire of devotion which ulti
 mately consumes the forest of our desires and leaves our consciousness fre
 e to soar untrammeled in infinite skies.”\n\n\n\n— Swami Kriyananda\,
  The Promise of Immortality\nWhat is devotion? How do we cultivate it in 
 our hearts and minds so the path to God is not littered with the debris of
  delusion?\n\nLet's dive into devotion and explore how\, when\, why\, and 
 where devotion fits into our lives.\n\nLed by Lorna\n\nThe fourth Tuesday 
 of the month is a FREE class in our Tuesday Yoga in Daily Life series.\n\n
 Register below and let us know you are coming!\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://anandaportland.org/wp-content/uploads/20
 24/05/HD-wallpaper-hanuman-with-open-heart-inside-of-rama-and-sita-hanuman
 .jpg
LOCATION:Ananda Portland Temple\, 4855 SW Watson Ave\, Beaverton\, OR\, 970
 05\, United States
