X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lewis Clark": "https://www.lclark.edu/live/events/390775-documentary-screening-silent-war-asian-american"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lewis_clark
X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
SUMMARY:Documentary Screening: Silent War\, Asian American Reckonings with
  Mental Health
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T180000
DTSTAMP:20260417T115957Z
UID:20260430T000000Z-390776@www.lclark.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T170000
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/482/width/80/height/80/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,2592,2596/112812_Silent_War_Poster_2026.rev.1776451091.png
DESCRIPTION:The AAPI ERG is hosting a screening of Silent War&#160\;from 5
 :00–7:00 p.m. in Corbett House Living Room 112. While all identities are
  welcome and encouraged to participate\, the focus of social will focus on
  supporting Asian\, Asian American\, and Pacific Islander identifying comm
 unities.RSVP Here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScsnJ7oiWvC5vl
 qF2sFLuKx_BXNSz8JDm9RSSNPEi3ZX0IKvA/viewform)Documentary Synopsis:Silent W
 ar: Asian American Reckonings with Mental Health is a groundbreaking docum
 entary that confronts the deep silence surrounding mental illness in Asian
  American communities. Through intimate stories of struggle\, survival\, a
 nd healing\, the film explores how cultural stigma\, intergenerational tra
 uma\, racism\, and systemic neglect have shaped the mental health experien
 ces of families from diverse Asian backgrounds. Featuring raw personal tes
 timonies\, expert insights\, and emotional family reckonings\, Silent War 
 reveals the human cost of staying silent—and the power of breaking that 
 silence. At once personal and political\, the film charts a collective jou
 rney from shame to resilience\, offering hope for a more inclusive and com
 passionate mental health future.  Questions about the documentary? Please 
 email Dr. Gon Ratanashevorn lc24-1138@lclark.edu.&#160\;
GEO:45.445206;-122.670893
LAST-MODIFIED:20260423T184242Z
LOCATION:Corbett House\, Living Room 112
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/live/events/390775-documentary-screening-silent
 -war-asian-american
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The AAPI ERG is hosting a screening of <
 em>Silent War&#160\;</em>from 5:00–7:00 p.m. in Corbett House Living Roo
 m 112. While all identities are welcome and encouraged to participate\, th
 e focus of social will focus on supporting Asian\, Asian American\, and Pa
 cific Islander identifying communities.</p><p style="text-align: center\;"
 ><a class="btn-small-style-1" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAI
 pQLScsnJ7oiWvC5vlqF2sFLuKx_BXNSz8JDm9RSSNPEi3ZX0IKvA/viewform">RSVP Here</
 a></p><p><strong>Documentary Synopsis:</strong></p><p><em>Silent War: Asia
 n American Reckonings with Mental Health</em> is a groundbreaking document
 ary that confronts the deep silence surrounding mental illness in Asian Am
 erican communities. Through intimate stories of struggle\, survival\, and 
 healing\, the film explores how cultural stigma\, intergenerational trauma
 \, racism\, and systemic neglect have shaped the mental health experiences
  of families from diverse Asian backgrounds. Featuring raw personal testim
 onies\, expert insights\, and emotional family reckonings\, Silent War rev
 eals the human cost of staying silent—and the power of breaking that sil
 ence. At once personal and political\, the film charts a collective journe
 y from shame to resilience\, offering hope for a more inclusive and compas
 sionate mental health future.</p><p>  Questions about the documentary? Ple
 ase email Dr. Gon Ratanashevorn lc24-1138@lclark.edu.&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:390776
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/482/width/80/heigh
 t/80/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,2592\,2596/112812_Silent_War_Poster_2026.rev.
 1776451091.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Silent War
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Join the Asian American and Pacific Islander (A
 API) ERG for a screening of <em>Silent War\,&#160\;</em>a powerful new doc
 umentary featuring Asian American voices confronting mental illness and th
 e impact of silence. The film explores shame\, resilience\, and hope for a
  more compassionate mental health future.&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/Los_Angeles
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
END:VEVENT
