X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
SUMMARY:ENVS Spring Poster Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T180000
DTSTAMP:20250507T091611Z
UID:20260501T000000Z-368314@www.lclark.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T170000
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/5/width/80/height/80/crop/1/s
 rc_region/0,0,1250,1250/112796_ENVS_AAESConf_SqLogo_030619.rev.1776266267.
 jpg
CATEGORIES:Open to the Public
DESCRIPTION:Please join us in celebrating the end of the semester and the 
 work that students have conducted in their ENVS and CORE courses this seme
 ster! The following classes will be represented in the poster celebration:
 ENVS 295 Environmental Engagement: Students will present public communicat
 ion materials they created using data collected during community mapping e
 ngagement methods in two Portland city parks - Gabriel Park and Irving Par
 k. The materials will both speak to engagement participant's perspective a
 nd experience with open and public space planning\, and inform the public 
 on how to engage with this topic further in Portland.&#160\;  ENVS 350 Env
 ironmental Theory: Students will present posters summarizing their environ
 mental praxis projects\, grounding a key theory concept in the real world.
   ENVS 400 Senior Seminar: Students will present individual posters on the
 ir capstone projects.  ENVS 400 Senior Seminar (North Portland capstone se
 ction): Students will present outcomes of their Albina-based senior enviro
 nmental research\, via individual posters and team-based StoryMaps and a n
 ew website\, us (http://albinamaps.us/).  ENVS 490 Landscape Mapping and M
 onitoring: Students will present their landscape mapping and monitoring re
 sults from semester long investigations in land use and land cover changes
 .  CORE 121 Measuring Environmental Meaning: Students will present posters
  summarizing the results of their original team-based environmental survey
 s.  CORE 121 Take Charge! Tackling Environmental Problems: Students will p
 resent posters summarizing their whole-class proposals for improving trans
 portation at LC.    This event will be held in Stamm\, in Fowler Student C
 enter. Snacks will be provided.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260415T182439Z
LOCATION:Stamm
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/368314-envs-poster-celeb
 ration
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Please join us in celebrating the end of
  the semester and the work that students have conducted in their ENVS and 
 CORE courses this semester! The following classes will be represented in t
 he poster celebration:</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS 295 Environmental Engagemen
 t</strong>: Students will present public communication materials they crea
 ted using data collected during community mapping engagement methods in tw
 o Portland city parks - Gabriel Park and Irving Park. The materials will b
 oth speak to engagement participant's perspective and experience with open
  and public space planning\, and inform the public on how to engage with t
 his topic further in Portland.&#160\;  </li><li><strong>ENVS 350 Environme
 ntal Theory</strong>: Students will present posters summarizing their envi
 ronmental praxis projects\, grounding a key theory concept in the real wor
 ld.  </li><li><strong>ENVS 400 Senior Seminar</strong>: Students will pres
 ent individual posters on their capstone projects.  </li><li><strong>ENVS 
 400 Senior Seminar (North Portland capstone section)</strong>: Students wi
 ll present outcomes of their Albina-based senior environmental research\, 
 via individual posters and team-based StoryMaps and a new website\, <a hre
 f="http://albinamaps.us/">us</a>.  </li><li><strong>ENVS 490 Landscape Map
 ping and Monitoring</strong>: Students will present their landscape mappin
 g and monitoring results from semester long investigations in land use and
  land cover changes.  </li><li><strong>CORE 121 Measuring Environmental Me
 aning</strong>: Students will present posters summarizing the results of t
 heir original team-based environmental surveys.  </li><li><strong>CORE 121
  Take Charge! Tackling Environmental Problems</strong>: Students will pres
 ent posters summarizing their whole-class proposals for improving transpor
 tation at LC.  </li></ul><p>  This event will be held in Stamm\, in Fowler
  Student Center. Snacks will be provided.</p>
