X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lewis Clark": "https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/381618-trauma-informed-clinical-supervision-online"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lewis_clark
X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
SUMMARY:Trauma-Informed Clinical Supervision (Online)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T100000
DTSTAMP:20260127T151911Z
UID:20260501T160000Z-381618@www.lclark.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T090000
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/91/width/80/height/80/crop/1/
 src_region/370,76,2717,2425/86005_Julianna_Vermeys.rev.1603837759.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The field of counseling and therapy stands at a crossroads: we
  must confront societal dysfunction and decide whether to challenge it or 
 perpetuate it.  As supervisors\, our role is to support clinicians' abilit
 y to acknowledge and utilize our privilege and power to better serve clien
 ts and communities. Once we look beyond pathologizing models\, we can ackn
 owledge the roles that society and other systems play in oppressing or emp
 owering our clients.  Clinicians and supervisors can promote equity by app
 lying integrated\, trauma-informed practices and care models that consider
  mental health\, neurodivergence\, socioeconomic status and racial factors
 \, while incorporating present-oriented\, strengths-based approaches.&#160
 \;  This training equips supervisors with practical skills and clinical to
 ols for trauma-informed supervision that can be used with both their super
 visees and the clients they serve.During this workshop participants will: 
      Learn integrative approaches to supervision that emphasize the need f
 or holistic self-awareness as a clinician          Explore the ethics of a
 uthenticity and therapeutic transparency to build trauma-informed trust\, 
 and encourage growth through interpersonal neurobiological safety         
  Examine factors that create obstacles to trauma-informed supervision and 
 develop strategies to reduce reactivity that may be passed on to clients  
   Details &amp\; RegistrationDate and Time: Friday\, May 1\, 2026\, 9 a.m.
 -1 p.m. PT\, OnlinePresenter:&#160\;Julianna Vermeys\, LPCCost and Credits
 : $105\, includes 4 CEUs. GSEC Alumni\, Adjuncts\, and Clinical Mental Hea
 lth Supervisors save 20%.&#160\;Register Online (https://lclark.tfaforms.n
 et/wf1W4MQ?epid=a1aUY000002IrRJ)Registration ends after Tuesday\, April 28
 thAccessibility: We are committed to making our events accessible to all n
 eeds and abilities. When registering\, please let us know your access need
 s. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or cce@lclark.edu (mailto:cce@lclark.edu)&#1
 60\;with questions.Please note: Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; 
 registrations are for current students only and do not include continuing 
 education credit (CEU/PDUs)About the InstructorJulianna Vermeys\, LPC has 
 been practicing integrative somatic psychotherapy since 2006. She is dedic
 ated to offering trauma-informed\, holistic therapy that addresses systemi
 c\, environmental and relational impacts through one's lifespan. Julianna 
 offers equitable\, existential and somatic oriented supervision clinical s
 upervision as an approved supervisor for the OBLPCT. She is inspired by fa
 mily/relationship dynamics\, attachment\, human development\, trauma-infor
 med healing and wellness\, and client-centered therapy rooted in compassio
 n and unconditional positive regard. She has specialized training in traum
 a-informed counseling\, mindfulness\, and body-based therapies. Julianna i
 s registered with Yoga Alliance as RYT 500-hr and is excited by the collec
 tive considerations of how we can embrace ancient practices from other cul
 tures with ethical\, conscious care. She teaches graduate classes as an ad
 junct faculty member at the Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School in the Coun
 seling Program\, and offers trainings for clinicians in trauma informed em
 bodiment practices to inform ethical clinical work and integrated somatic 
 psychotherapy.New workshops and trainings are added to our calendar regula
 rly. For the latest on professional development related to your specific i
 nterests\, sign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735
 441)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T205009Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/381618-trauma-informed-c
 linical-supervision-online
