 istrations are for current students only and <strong>do not</strong> inclu
 de continuing education credit (CEU/PDUs)</em></p></div></li></ul></div><h
 r /><h2><strong>About the Instructor</strong></h2><p style="line-height: 1
 .5\;"><strong>Julianna Vermeys\, LPC</strong> has been practicing integrat
 ive somatic psychotherapy since 2006. She is dedicated to offering trauma-
 informed\, holistic therapy that addresses systemic\, environmental and re
 lational impacts through one's lifespan. Julianna offers equitable\, exist
 ential and somatic oriented supervision clinical supervision as an approve
 d supervisor for the OBLPCT. She is inspired by family/relationship dynami
 cs\, attachment\, human development\, trauma-informed healing and wellness
 \, and client-centered therapy rooted in compassion and unconditional posi
 tive regard. She has specialized training in trauma-informed counseling\, 
 mindfulness\, and body-based therapies. Julianna is registered with Yoga A
 lliance as RYT 500-hr and is excited by the collective considerations of h
 ow we can embrace ancient practices from other cultures with ethical\, con
 scious care. She teaches graduate classes as an adjunct faculty member at 
 the Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School in the Counseling Program\, and off
 ers trainings for clinicians in trauma informed embodiment practices to in
 form ethical clinical work and integrated somatic psychotherapy.</p><div i
