BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b5908e23b45fff20f1ed92"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:One Book One Coast Book Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T200000
UID:69b5908e23b45fff20f1ed92@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the largest book club on the West Coast!\nWest Slo
 pe Community Library will be hosting a discussion of\nThey Called Us Enemy
 \nby George Takei.\nOne Book\, One Coast\nis a collaborative program uniti
 ng a wide network of West Coast libraries in a shared celebration of liter
 acy\, learning\, community\, and civil discourse. From April 1 through May
  31st\, all participating libraries will read and discuss\nThey Called Us 
 Enemy\nby George Takei.\nThey Called Us Enemy\nis a graphic memoir recount
 ing actor/author/activist George Takei’s childhood imprisoned within Ame
 rican concentration camps during World War II. Confronting questions of pa
 triotism\, family\, loyalty\, and community\, George’s work is a stunnin
 g examination of what it means to be American\, both then and now.\nRead\n
 They Called Us Enemy\nat WCCLS\nNote: The library closes at 5:00. When you
  arrive\, please ring the bell at the door to the right of the main entran
 ce.
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library\, The library closes at 5:00. When y
 ou arrive\, please ring the bell at the door to the right of the main entr
 ance.﻿﻿
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b5908e23b45fff20f1ed92
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ohsu Library": "https://librarycalendar.ohsu.edu/event/16571477"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ohsu_library
X-SOURCE:Ohsu Library
DTSTART:20260501T190000Z
DTEND:20260501T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260501T000000Z
SUMMARY:Supercharge Your Research with Scite AI
DESCRIPTION:Discover how Scite AI can elevate your research process by 
 combining the power of generative AI with a scholarly literature citation 
 database. This session introduces key features of Scite AI\, including the 
 Scite Assistant for summarizing literature\, Table mode for constructing 
 evidence tables\, and Dashboards for targeted literature analysis. Ethical 
 considerations and comparisons to similar tools will also be 
 addressed.\n\nLearning Objectives:\n\nAfter this session\, learners will be 
 able to:\n\n\n	Use Scite AI for research\n	\n		Discover literature using 
 citation searching\n		Summarize search results with the AI 
 Assistant\n		Query a specific body of literature using 
 Dashboards\n	\n	\n	Describe limitations of Scite and potential ethical 
 concerns \n	Compare Scite AI with similar tools\n\n\nThis workshop will be 
 recorded\, and the recording will be shared with all registered attendees 
 after the session. If you cannot make the workshop date and time\, you are 
 welcome to register in order to receive a copy of the recording.
LOCATION:Virtual
ORGANIZER;CN="Brandon Wilkinson":MAILTO:wilkinbr@ohsu.edu
CATEGORIES:AI
UID:LibCal-6248-16571477
URL:https://librarycalendar.ohsu.edu/event/16571477
END:VEVENT
