 /src_region/0,0,1080,1080/104459_Belong..rev.1720032412.png
DESCRIPTION:What does faith have to say about Belonging?  Whether at a his
 torically religious institution or at a secular school\, religion influenc
 es our approaches to inclusion and difference.  Associations serving relig
 iously affiliated colleges and universities play a vital role in helping i
 nstitutions remain grounded in mission while managing the changing landsca
 pe of higher education. This webinar will explore observations from associ
 ations serving religious institutions and how their campuses are navigatin
 g the intersection of faith\, identity\, and belonging.  Featuring leaders
  from associations that represent diverse religious traditions\, the conve
 rsation will highlight strategies\, resources\, and approaches that help i
 nstitutions stay true to their founding values and foster supportive envir
 onments for their students. Panelists will share how they see campuses mov
 e through complex questions around mission alignment\, student engagement\
 , and community building.  Attendees will gain insight into:Approaches to 
 supporting student belonging within faith-based frameworks  Examples of pr
 ograms\, initiatives\, and resources offered to member campuses  Opportuni
 ties for collaboration and shared learning across institutions    Featurin
 g:Donna Carroll\, Association of Catholic Colleges and Universities  David
  Hoag\, Council for Christian Colleges &amp\; Universities  Lamont Anthony
  Wells\, Network of Evangelical Lutheran Church in American (ELCA) College
 s and Universities  Register Here (https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/registe
 r/WN_mFCNRzOsTpCbyUkL3D8Isw?ampDeviceId=bfd0eac0-929f-4dd5-8074-8cc2b672cd
 15&amp\;ampSessionId=1775576497642&amp\;ampDeviceId=bfd0eac0-929f-4dd5-807
