X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  What does faith have to say about Belong
 ing?</p><p>  Whether at a historically religious institution or at a secul
 ar school\, religion influences our approaches to inclusion and difference
 .</p><p>  Associations serving religiously affiliated colleges and univers
 ities play a vital role in helping institutions remain grounded in mission
  while managing the changing landscape of higher education. This webinar w
 ill explore observations from associations serving religious institutions 
 and how their campuses are navigating the intersection of faith\, identity
 \, and belonging.</p><p>  Featuring leaders from associations that represe
 nt diverse religious traditions\, the conversation will highlight strategi
 es\, resources\, and approaches that help institutions stay true to their 
 founding values and foster supportive environments for their students. Pan
 elists will share how they see campuses move through complex questions aro
 und mission alignment\, student engagement\, and community building.</p><p
 >  Attendees will gain insight into:</p><ol><li>Approaches to supporting s
 tudent belonging within faith-based frameworks  </li><li>Examples of progr
 ams\, initiatives\, and resources offered to member campuses  </li><li>Opp
 ortunities for collaboration and shared learning across institutions  </li
 ></ol><p>  Featuring:</p><ul><li>Donna Carroll\, Association of Catholic C
 olleges and Universities  </li><li>David Hoag\, Council for Christian Coll
 eges &amp\; Universities  </li><li>Lamont Anthony Wells\, Network of Evang
 elical Lutheran Church in American (ELCA) Colleges and Universities  </li>
 </ul><p style="text-align: center\;"><a class="btn-small-style-1" href="ht
 tps://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_mFCNRzOsTpCbyUkL3D8Isw?ampDevice
