DESCRIPTION:Valerie Gillis goes missing in Maine while hiking the Appalach
 ian Trail. The mystery at the center of this addictive novel is complement
 ed by vibrant descriptions of Valerie’s environment\, endearing portraya
 ls of the characters involved in her search\, and moving explorations of c
 omplex mother-daughter relationships.\nReserve it\nhere\n:  Also available
  in large print\, eBook\, downloadable audiobook\, and audiobook CD\nIf yo
 u would like to read ahead\, here is the book club’s schedule for the re
 st of 2026:\nMay 6th (online) & 7th (in person) -\nHeartwood\nby Amity Gai
 ge\nJune 3rd (online) & 4th (in person) -\nThe Anthropocene Reviewed\nby J
 ohn Green\nJuly & August - Break\nSeptember 9th (online) & 10th (in person
 ) -\nTress of the Emerald Sea\nby Brandon Sanderson\nOctober 7th (online) 
 & 8th (in person) -\nRemarkably Bright Creatures\nby Shelby Van Pelt\nNove
 mber 4th (online) & 5th (in person) -\nBad Cree\nby Jessica Johns\nDecembe
 r - Break
