BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lewis Clark": "https://www.lclark.edu/live/events/389944-relax-and-rejuvenate-sound-bath-and-meditation"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lewis_clark
X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
SUMMARY:Relax and Rejuvenate: Sound Bath and Meditation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T160000
DTSTAMP:20260417T113123Z
UID:20260520T213000Z-390774@www.lclark.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T143000
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/482/width/80/height/80/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,1500,1500/112754_Relax_and_Rejuvenate_Sound_Bath_and_Medit
 ation.rev.1775849503.png
DESCRIPTION:Sound Bath Experience  Allow yourself to surrender to the heal
 ing power of sound\, creating space for peace\, renewal\, and deep inner h
 armony. This offering begins with a brief guided meditation\, followed by 
 an extended Sound Bath featuring the resonant tones of crystal bowls and o
 ther healing instruments. The soothing frequencies help promote deep relax
 ation\, renewal\, and overall physical and emotional well-being.What to Ex
 pect:Introduction and Intention Setting – A short meditation to center t
 he mind and prepare for the journey.  Sound Bath – Experience the immers
 ive power of sound as vibrations wash over you\, supporting deep rest and 
 energetic balance.  Closing and Integration – Time for reflection\, gent
 le reawakening\, and optional sharing.  What to Bring:  To enhance your co
 mfort\, we recommend bringing:A yoga mat\, blanket\, pillow\, and eye mask
 —whatever supports you in fully relaxing while lying down for an hour.  
 A small personal item for the altar to honor someone or something\, set an
  intention\, or infuse with positive energy.  Seats are limited! We have r
 oom for 15 faculty/staff participants for this event. We will enable a wai
 tlist if we reach that cap.
GEO:45.4506477144909;-122.671172383575
LAST-MODIFIED:20260417T183132Z
LOCATION:Gregg Pavilion
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/live/events/389944-relax-and-rejuvenate-sound-b
 ath-and-meditation
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;"><strong>Sound B
 ath Experience</strong></p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Allow yourself 
 to surrender to the healing power of sound\, creating space for peace\, re
 newal\, and deep inner harmony. This offering begins with a brief guided m
 editation\, followed by an extended Sound Bath featuring the resonant tone
 s of crystal bowls and other healing instruments. The soothing frequencies
  help promote deep relaxation\, renewal\, and overall physical and emotion
 al well-being.</p><p><strong>What to Expect:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>I
 ntroduction and Intention Setting</strong> – A short meditation to cente
 r the mind and prepare for the journey.  </li><li><strong>Sound Bath</stro
 ng> – Experience the immersive power of sound as vibrations wash over yo
 u\, supporting deep rest and energetic balance.  </li><li><strong>Closing 
 and Integration</strong> – Time for reflection\, gentle reawakening\, an
 d optional sharing.  </li></ul><p><strong>What to Bring:</strong></p><p>  
 To enhance your comfort\, we recommend bringing:</p><ul><li>A yoga mat\, b
 lanket\, pillow\, and eye mask—whatever supports you in fully relaxing w
 hile lying down for an hour.  </li><li>A small personal item for the altar
  to honor someone or something\, set an intention\, or infuse with positiv
 e energy.  </li></ul><p><em><strong>Seats are limited! We have room for 15
  faculty/staff participants for this event. We will enable a waitlist if w
 e reach that cap.</strong></em></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:390774
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/482/width/80/heigh
 t/80/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1500\,1500/112754_Relax_and_Rejuvenate_Sound_
 Bath_and_Meditation.rev.1775849503.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:relax and rejuvenate sound bath
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  As the semester has come to an end\, the Office
  of Equity and Inclusion invites faculty and staff to reflect on the acade
 mic year\, relax\, and build community with a year end sound bath and medi
 tation opportunity.<br />\n  <br />\n  The session will be led by <a href=
 "https://crownandhearthealing.com/">Laura Yee of Crown &amp\; Heart Healin
 g</a>\, on May 20 from 2:30–4:00 p.m. in Gregg Pavilion. Space is limite
 d\, RSVP if you would like to attend!\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/Los_Angeles
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Multcolib": "https://multcolib.org/events-classes/teen-drop-get-creative-makerspace-129"}
X-SOURCE-ID:multcolib
SUMMARY:Teen drop-in: Get creative at the makerspace!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T173000
UID:2fcecef9dc20927e4f2cdcb7a9e90795@multcolib.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://multcolib.org/sites/default/files/styles
 /medium/public/2026-04/Generic_Makerspace_3D_Print.jpg?itok=y6ViLT3p
DESCRIPTION:Calling all teens in grades 6-12! Come make something cool\, l
 earn a new skill\, and meet friendly people in this teen-focused creative 
 space. Makerspace staff and volunteers will teach you how to use our tech 
 equipment to design things and express yourself. Project examples include 
 3D printers\, craft cutters\, sewing machines\, custom t shirts and tote b
