X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Kathak: Classical Dance from Northern India
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T104500
UID:69d179d69057005337d27dd3@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:We are celebrating Asian American and Pacific Islander month w
 ith  Kathak\, a dance style from Northern India\, featuring the talent of 
 Shivani Joshi. Kathak is one of the eight major forms of Indian classical
  dance based on scenes from the life of Krishna.\nAt this event you and yo
 ur family will experience the beauty\, expressive\, and vibrant movements 
 based in rhythm accompanied by traditional music of India.\nLearn more ab
 out Shivani Joshi\,\nhere\n.\nEveryone welcome!\nNo registration required.
 \nThis is an all ages event.
LOCATION:Sherwood Public Library\, Community Room\, main floor.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d179d69057005337d27dd3
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c422465a2d780f42c4b52f"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Makerspace Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T130000
UID:69c422465a2d780f42c4b52f@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Makerspace Open Labs are for anyone who wants to check out the
  space and use our equipment to make cool things. Room assistants are avai
 lable to guide you in the basic use of the tools and technology. Come in w
 ith an idea and leave with a finished project! For more information about 
 the Makerspace and its resources\,\nsee here\n.\nMakerspace Open Labs take
  place on the following weekly schedule:\nTuesdays\n\, 5:30 - 7:30PM\nThur
 sdays\n\, 4:00 - 6:00PM\nSaturdays\n\, 10:00 AM - 1:00PM\nSundays\n\, 1:30
  - 5:30P\nEach month we provide the materials\, tools and instructions for
  a featured Makerspace project that everyone is invited to try.\nMay's fea
 tured project is Galaxy Rings.\nIMPORTANT:\nAdults using the Makerspace fo
 r the first time need to\nsign a waiver\n\; people under the age of 18 mus
 t have a waiver signed by a parent or guardian.\nYou can sign and submit w
 aivers online here.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c422465a2d780f42c4b52f
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
