X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Digital Navigator Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T153000
UID:69c85287e2a2952aed0b4b15@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you need one-on-one assistance with your digital questions?
  A trusted guide can help you learn about home connectivity\, devices\, an
 d digital skills. Register for a slot. Bring your device or use a library 
 computer.\nRegistrants will be contacted for more details.\nSlots are 30-4
 0 minutes long. Sign up for your preferred time slot: 3\, 3:45\, 4:30\, or
  5:15. [We do not have a waitlist\; please call or visit the library the 
 day off the Digital Navigator appointment to check availability.]\nThe Dig
 ital Navigator Program (DNP) is a free service made possible by a partners
 hip between Washington County Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the
  American Connections Corps\, who empowers its members and the communities
  they serve to address digital disparities and create lasting change.
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, Enter via the rec center's main e
 ntrance and walk through the building to the library. Or use the doorbell 
 at the door by the library.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c85287e2a2952aed0b4b15
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WCCLS Libraries": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698655718b29ea2800ce6915"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698655718b29ea2800ce6914"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:One Book\, One Coast
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T151500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T163000
UID:698655718b29ea2800ce6914@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a library program uniting a network of West Coast 
 Libraries in a shared celebration of literacy\, learning\, community and c
 ivil discourse.\nThe One Book\, One Coast 2026 chosen title is "They Calle
 d Us the Enemy" by George Takei.  We will kick off this program by explor
 ing the traditional Japanese method of fish printing called Gyotaku (don't
  worry\, we're not using real fish!).  We will have copies of the book av
 ailable to hand out at the art event.  Later\, we will discuss the book a
 nd attend a live-stream author talk with George Takei.\nThursday April 16:
   Gyotaku Fish Printing and book handout\nTeen group 3:15pm-4:30pm\nAdult
  group 6:30pm-8:00pm\nThursday May 28:  Book Discussion\nTeen group 3:15p
 m-4:30pm\nAdult group 6:30pm-8:00pm\nSunday May 31:  Live-Stream Author T
 alk with George Takei\n2:00pm-4:00pm
LOCATION:Banks Public Library\, Jane Moore Community Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698655718b29ea2800ce6914
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
