 We are committed to making our events accessible to all needs and abilitie
 s. When registering\, please let us know your access needs. Contact us at 
 503-768-6040 or <a href="mailto:cce@lclark.edu">cce@lclark.edu</a>&#160\;w
 ith questions.<br/></em></p><p class="p1" style="font-size: 15px\; line-he
 ight: 1.5\;"><em><strong>Please note:</strong> Discounted &#x2018\;Student
  Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for current students only and <strong>do 
 not</strong> include continuing education credit (CEU/PDUs)</em></p></div>
 </li></ul></div><hr /><h2><strong>About the Instructors</strong></h2><p st
 yle="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Carson Varnum\, MEd\,</strong> (he/him) i
 s a community builder and educator with an expertise in sexual health\, se
 xualities\, peer education\, and community development. Carson specializes
  in building capacity in sex educators\, creating sexuality education and 
 leadership development programming for adolescents\, and developing progra
 ms that center Queer and Trans communities. Carson works at Lewis &amp\; C
 lark Graduate School as TransActives's Head of Education and Outreach\, wh
 ere he supports transgender\, non-binary\, and other gender expansive yout
 h by strengthening the systems that surround them. He received his Masters
  of Education in Human Sexuality from Widener University in 2012 and is cu
 rrently a PhD student in Education and Leadership at Pacific University. C
 arson is a big fan of being on mountains\, in rivers\, and with friends.&#
