SUMMARY:Trauma and Grief in Kids and Teens: How to Facilitate Healing and 
 Growth
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T120000
UID:69a21d7b4dacf581ff7e708b@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn about the impact of trauma\, stress\, and grief on kids 
 and teens\, and how to foster adaptive processing and adjustment to stress
 ful events. We will discuss when and where to seek professional help with 
 time for Q&A. Presented by: Julia Ross\, Psy.D.\, and Karina Peters\, Psy.
 D.\, Children's Program. This program is part of our Parent Information Se
 ries. Adults only.\nRegistration is required. We will send you a Zoom lin
 k via email an hour before the class begins.\nPresented by the Cedar Mill 
 and Bethany Community Libraries.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a21d7b4dacf581ff7e708b
