BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"University Of Portland": "https://calendar.up.edu/event/catholic-education-and-artificial-intelligence"}
X-SOURCE-ID:university_of_portland
X-SOURCE:University Of Portland
CATEGORIES:Academic,Conference / Symposium
DESCRIPTION:REGISTRATION IS OPEN!\n\nEarly Bird Registration is happening n
 ow and affordable\, on campus lodging is available to reserve until May 15t
 h! \n\n \n\nBuilding on Our Foundation: From Principles to Practice \n\nFol
 lowing our inaugural conference's resounding success with participants from
  19 Catholic institutions\, we return with deeper insights and practical to
 ols as AI reshapes education at inhuman speed. Since our first gathering in
  October of 2024\, AI has fundamentally transformed academic landscapes—fro
 m research methodologies to student services\, from classroom instruction t
 o campus operations. \n\nThis year's conference emphasizes hands-on learnin
 g and specialized application\, featuring expanded workshops and targeted b
 reakout sessions designed for your specific role and discipline\, ensuring 
 you leave with immediately applicable strategies and tools. \n\n \n\nWHAT'S
  NEW FOR 2026\n\nHands-On Workshop Format\n\nMove beyond theoretical discus
 sions to practical application with interactive sessions featuring the late
 st AI tools and implementation strategies.\n\nSpecialized Learning Tracks\n
 \nChoose your path based on your role and area of expertise\, with dedicate
 d sessions for deeper\, targeted learning.\n\nCurrent AI Landscape Focus\n\
 nAddress the rapid developments since 2024\, including:\n\nAdvanced AI tool
 s in research and scholarshipUpdated academic integrity frameworksAI's role
  in student mental health and formationInstitutional policies for responsib
 le AI adoptionPreparing graduates for an AI-integrated workforce \n\nThe Co
 llege of Arts and Sciences and the Dundon-Berchtold Institute for Moral For
 mation and Applied Ethics at the University of Portland are pleased to host
  this essential gathering. As an independently governed Catholic university
  guided by the Congregation of Holy Cross\, the University of Portland cont
 inues its mission of teaching and learning\, faith and formation\, and serv
 ice and leadership in addressing the critical intersection of technology an
 d human dignity. \n\n \n\nThank you to our conference sponsors!
DTSTAMP:20260425T021153Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260603
GEO:45.571791;-122.724529
LOCATION:University of Portland
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Catholic Education and Artificial Intelligence: Principled Educatio
 nal Leadership for the AI Revolution 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51082552012963
URL:https://calendar.up.edu/event/catholic-education-and-artificial-intelli
 gence
END:VEVENT
