BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lewis Clark": "https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/380080-family-therapy-in-the-treatment-of-eating-disorders-o"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lewis_clark
X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
SUMMARY:Family Therapy in the Treatment of Eating Disorders (Online)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T173000
DTSTAMP:20260115T113514Z
UID:20260620T160000Z-380080@www.lclark.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T090000
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/91/width/80/height/80/crop/1/
 src_region/0,0,1800,3200/93879_Curling_Leaves_-_pexels-joey-kyber-119591.r
 ev.1649880761.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This course will cover the topic of disordered eating and eati
 ng disorders in children.  Family therapy treatment strategies including t
 he Maudsley method and other approaches will be discussed.  Additional foc
 us will be placed on ways to foster healthy eating and positive lifestyle 
 choices in families.  This course is part of our Eating Disorder Certifica
 te Program (https://www.lclark.edu/programs/continuing_education/certifica
 tes/eating_disorders/).Course Details &amp\; RegistrationDates: Saturday &
 amp\; Sunday\, June 20-21\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-5:30 p.m.\, PT\, OnlineInstructo
 r: Dianne Lamberty Rogers\, LMFT\, CADCCurrent Students and Certificate Ca
 ndidates: CECP 878-21\, 1 semester hour of Graduate Continuing Education c
 redit\, $385.&#160\;Individual Class: We welcome students seeking to take 
 individual courses within the certificate program. Admission to the progra
 m is required. Click here for more information (https://www.lclark.edu/pro
 grams/continuing_education/certificates/eating_disorders/#Admission)Regist
 er Online (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735425)We are committed to making 
 our events accessible to all needs and abilities. If you have a disability
  that may impact your academic performance\, you may request accommodation
 s by meeting with the Office of Student Accessibility staff and submitting
  documentation on the Office of Student Accessibility website (/offices/st
 udent-accessibility/). Please be aware that the process for evaluation and
  implementation of accommodations could take 2-3 weeks\, so please be in t
 ouch with the OSA as soon as possible. Email access@lclark.edu (mailto:acc
 ess@lclark.edu) with any additional questions or concerns.About the Instru
 ctor  Dianne Lamberty Rogers\, LMFT\, CADC has been a therapist serving ki
 ds\, families and adults since completing her Masters in Marriage Couple a
 nd Family Therapy at Lewis and Clark Graduate School in 2015. Dianne has s
 pecialized in working with disordered eating and body image issues\, famil
 ies of clients with eating disorders\, and Spanish speaking families.  Dia
 nne has worked with youth and families in school based\, intensive in-home
 \, and outpatient settings providing drug\, alcohol\, and mental health tr
 eatment\, and also in intensive outpatient and partial hospitalization set
 tings for eating disorders. Dianne's work has included working with incarc
 erated youth\, DHS-involved families\, and foster and adopted youth.  Dian
 ne conducts all of her work using a trauma informed and culturally compete
 nt lens as well as a body liberation standpoint. Dianne teaches the Family
  Therapy in the Treatment of Eating Disorders course in the Eating Disorde
 rs Certificate Program at Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School. She is also 
 a Clinical Supervisor to Lewis and Clark and other graduate interns at You
 th Contact Inc.New workshops and trainings are added to our calendar regul
 arly. For the latest on professional development related to your specific 
 interests\, sign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/473
 5441)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260323T184034Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/380080-family-therapy-in
 -the-treatment-of-eating-disorders-o
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  This course w
 ill cover the topic of disordered eating and eating disorders in children.
 </p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Family therapy treatment strategies in
 cluding the Maudsley method and other approaches will be discussed.</p><p 
 style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Additional focus will be placed on ways to fo
 ster healthy eating and positive lifestyle choices in families.</p><p styl
 e="line-height: 1.5\;">  This course is part of our <a href="https://www.l
 clark.edu/programs/continuing_education/certificates/eating_disorders/" ta
 rget="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Eating Disorder Certificate Progra
 m</a>.</p><hr /><h2 class="p1"><strong>Course Details &amp\; Registration<
 /strong></h2><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Dates:</strong> Saturda
 y &amp\; Sunday\, June 20-21\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-5:30 p.m.\, PT\, Online</p><p
  style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Instructor:</strong> Dianne Lamberty R
 ogers\, LMFT\, CADC</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Current Stude
 nts and Certificate Candidates:</strong> CECP 878-21\, 1 semester hour of 
 Graduate Continuing Education credit\, $385.&#160\;</p><p style="line-heig
 ht: 1.5\;"><strong>Individual Class:</strong> We welcome students seeking 
 to take individual courses within the certificate program. Admission to th
 e program is required. <strong><a href="https://www.lclark.edu/programs/co
 ntinuing_education/certificates/eating_disorders/#Admission">Click here fo
 r more information</a></strong></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\; text-align
 : center\;"><strong><a class="btn-small-style-1" href="https://lclark.tfaf
 orms.net/4735425" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Register Online</a></stro
 ng></p><div id="lw_widget_c96ec80c" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs
  lw_widget_blurbs lw_widget_id_8625 lw_widget_accessibility_statement_ce_r
 egistration lw_widget_pagination"><ul class="lw_widget_results lw_widget_r
 esults_blurbs"><li class="lw_item_1"><div class="lw_blurbs_body"><p class=
 "p1" style="font-size: 15px\; line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>We are committed
  to making our events accessible to all needs and abilities.</strong> If y
 ou have a disability that may impact your academic performance\, you may r
 equest accommodations by meeting with the Office of Student Accessibility 
 staff and submitting documentation on the <a href="https://www.lclark.edu/
 offices/student-accessibility/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Office of S
 tudent Accessibility website</a>. Please be aware that the process for eva
 luation and implementation of accommodations could take 2-3 weeks\, so ple
 ase be in touch with the OSA as soon as possible. Email <a href="mailto:ac
 cess@lclark.edu">access@lclark.edu</a> with any additional questions or co
 ncerns.</p></div></li></ul></div><hr /><h2><strong>About the Instructor</s
 trong></h2><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Dianne Lamberty Rogers\, LMFT\,
  CADC has been a therapist serving kids\, families and adults since comple
 ting her Masters in Marriage Couple and Family Therapy at Lewis and Clark 
 Graduate School in 2015. Dianne has specialized in working with disordered
  eating and body image issues\, families of clients with eating disorders\
 , and Spanish speaking families.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Dianne
  has worked with youth and families in school based\, intensive in-home\, 
 and outpatient settings providing drug\, alcohol\, and mental health treat
 ment\, and also in intensive outpatient and partial hospitalization settin
 gs for eating disorders. Dianne's work has included working with incarcera
 ted youth\, DHS-involved families\, and foster and adopted youth.</p><p st
 yle="line-height: 1.5\;">  Dianne conducts all of her work using a trauma 
 informed and culturally competent lens as well as a body liberation standp
 oint. Dianne teaches the Family Therapy in the Treatment of Eating Disorde
 rs course in the Eating Disorders Certificate Program at Lewis &amp\; Clar
 k Graduate School. She is also a Clinical Supervisor to Lewis and Clark an
 d other graduate interns at Youth Contact Inc.</p><div id="lw_widget_470b3
 9ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_blurbs lw_widget_id_
 3994 lw_widget_opt_in lw_widget_pagination"><ul class="lw_widget_results l
 w_widget_results_blurbs"><li class="lw_item_1"><div class="lw_blurbs_body"
 ><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em><strong>New workshops and trainings are
  added to our calendar regularly.</strong> For the latest on professional 
 development related to your specific interests\, <a href="https://lclark.t
 faforms.net/4735441">sign up for our mailing list!</a></em></p></div></li>
 </ul></div>
