URL:https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/387513-applied-suicide-i
 ntervention-skills-training-asist-in
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  The Applied S
 uicide Intervention Skills Training (ASIST) is an intensive\, interactive 
 and practice-dominated course for those who want to feel more comfortable\
 , confident and competent in providing <span style="background-color: tran
 sparent\;">an intervention with someone who is having thoughts of suicide.
 &#160\;</span></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><span class="s1">This work
 shop will provide extensive opportunities for supported skills practice an
 d shared participant experiences that enrich learning.</span></p><p style=
 "line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>After this workshop\, participants will have 
 an increased ability to:</strong></p><ul><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"
 >      Recognize when someone may be thinking about suicide    </p></li><l
 i><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Provide a skilled intervention\, inc
 luding connect the person to further support    </p></li><li><p style="lin
 e-height: 1.5\;">      Guide the development of a safety plan through a co
 llaborative\, helping relationship    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 
 1.5\;">      Consider how personal and community attitudes about suicide a
 ffect someone's openness to seek help and the caregiver's ability to provi
 de it    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Reduce suicide s
 tigma and build confidence and capacity to provide suicide first aid<br />
 <br /></p></li></ul><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Who should atten
 d?</strong> The training is for anyone in a position of trust\, including 
 mental health and addictions professionals\, school psychologists\, school
  counselors\, educators\, healthcare workers\, peer support and recovery s
 pecialists\, housing specialists\, law enforcement\, faith leaders\, and c
 ommunity volunteers.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  "<em>Prior to part
 icipating in ASIST\, I was reluctant to get involved in conversations invo
 lving suicide because I felt uneasy about how to engage effectively. I wal
 ked away from this training with clear and applicable tools to enter a con
 versation with confidence and fearlessness\, equipped to support and conve
 rse openly about suicide. It was absolutely one of the most valuable train
 ings I have experienced in my career.</em>"</p><p>  - Counselor\, Roosevel
 t High School</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Training credits ar
 e NASP and NASW-approved for Continuing Professional Development (CPD).</s
 trong></p><hr /><h2><strong>Details &amp\; Registration</strong></h2><p st
 yle="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Dates and Time:</strong> Friday &amp\; Sa
 turday\, June 26-27\, 2026\, 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m.&#160\;</p><p style="line-
 height: 1.5\;"><strong>Location:</strong> Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate Scho
 ol\, South Chapel and York 107</p><p><strong>Instructors:</strong> Leslie 
 Rodgers\, and Kathy Wilson-Fey</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Co
 st and Credits:</strong> $350\, includes 15 NASP-Approved CEUs or PDUs (12
 .75 NASW Credits). Alumni\, Adjuncts\, and GSEC Clinical Mental Health Sup
 ervisors save 20%.&#160\;</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong><a clas
 s="btn-small-style-1" href="https://lclark.tfaforms.net/wf1W4MQ?epid=a1aUY
 000002Unrl">Register Online</a></strong></p><div id="lw_widget_30f0017c" c
 lass="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_blurbs lw_widget_id_7119 l
 w_widget_accessibility_statement lw_widget_pagination"><ul class="lw_widge
 t_results lw_widget_results_blurbs"><li class="lw_item_1"><div class="lw_b
 lurbs_body"><p class="p1" style="font-size: 15px\; line-height: 1.5\;"><em
 ><strong>Accessibility:</strong> We are committed to making our events acc
 essible to all needs and abilities. When registering\, please let us know 
 your access needs. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or <a href="mailto:cce@lclar
 k.edu">cce@lclark.edu</a>&#160\;with questions.<br/></em></p><p class="p1"
  style="font-size: 15px\; line-height: 1.5\;"><em><strong>Please note:</st
 rong> Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for curr
 ent students only and <strong>do not</strong> include continuing education
  credit (CEU/PDUs)</em></p></div></li></ul></div><hr /><h2><strong>About t
 he Instructors</strong></h2><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Leslie R
 odgers</strong> is a licensed clinical social worker and registered ASIST 
 (Applied Suicide Intervention Skills) trainer with over 20 years experienc
 e working with children and adults in various therapeutic settings\, inclu
 ding group homes\, psychiatric hospitals\, and schools. Her current work h
 as involved implementing best practice procedures and providing staff deve
 lopment in student threat assessment\, suicide prevention\, and crisis res
 ponse for school districts. She holds a BA from the University of Texas an
 d a Masters in Social Work from Portland State University.</p><p style="li
 ne-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Kathy Wilson-Fey</strong> is a registered ASIST 
 Trainer and has clinical therapy and teaching experience in a variety of s
 ettings\, including community college\, community mental health\, and an i
 nternational university. She has 15 years of experience as a mental health
  specialist in public schools\, where she worked with students and familie
 s\, trained school staff on suicide intervention\, and coordinated school 
 support during crises. Kathy is fluent in Spanish and is committed to equi
 ty work and cultural competence. She holds a BA from Whitman College and a
  Masters in Counseling Psychology from the University of Oregon.</p><div i
 d="lw_widget_470b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_bl
 urbs lw_widget_id_3994 lw_widget_opt_in lw_widget_pagination"><ul class="l
 w_widget_results lw_widget_results_blurbs"><li class="lw_item_1"><div clas
 s="lw_blurbs_body"><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em><strong>New workshops
  and trainings are added to our calendar regularly.</strong> For the lates
 t on professional development related to your specific interests\, <a href
 ="https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441">sign up for our mailing list!</a></
 em></p></div></li></ul></div>
