 w="855" data-max-h="856" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></picture> 
 Krystal Marcinkiewicz\, MA\, LPC\, LMHC is a Licensed Professional Counsel
 or and Clinical Supervisor\, having earned her Masters Degree in Professio
 nal Mental Health Counseling from Lewis &amp\; Clark College in 2018. Draw
 ing from an integrative feminist approach\, her work is grounded in person
 -centered values\, emphasizing authentic connection\, and collaborative en
 gagement. Her primary clinical focus is supporting clients in navigating i
 dentity development\, body politics\, neurodivergence\, emotional codepend
 ency\, highly sensitive personalities and other complex emotional experien
 ces.</p><p style="line-height: 1.6\;">  In addition to clinical work\, Kry
 stal is also passionate in training and mentoring emerging counselors. She
  is an adjunct professor\, teaching a wide variety of graduate counseling 
 courses with an underlying emphasis on counselor identity development\, re
 flective practice\, and cultivating professional resilience.</p><p style="
 line-height: 1.6\;">  In both the classroom\, and her clinical work\, Krys
 tal is committed to creating affirming spaces that honor intersectional id
 entities and lived experience.</p><div id="lw_widget_470b39ba" class="lw_w
 idget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_blurbs lw_widget_id_3994 lw_widget_o
 pt_in lw_widget_pagination"><ul class="lw_widget_results lw_widget_results
 _blurbs"><li class="lw_item_1"><div class="lw_blurbs_body"><p style="line-
 height: 1.5\;"><em><strong>New workshops and trainings are added to our ca
 lendar regularly.</strong> For the latest on professional development rela
 ted to your specific interests\, <a href="https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735
 441">sign up for our mailing list!</a></em></p></div></li></ul></div>
