BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lewis Clark": "https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/388399-cultivating-spaciousness-and-abundance-courage-to-lea"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lewis_clark
X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
SUMMARY:Cultivating Spaciousness and Abundance: Courage to Lead® for Sust
 ainable Growth (Online)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260709
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTSTAMP:20260327T103436Z
UID:20260709T070000Z-388399@www.lclark.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20260709
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/91/width/80/height/80/crop/1/
 src_region/0,0,3200,2133/112590_ralphs_fotos-flowers-3598555.rev.177463531
 5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:As leaders we are often called to come from a place of perpetu
 al productivity\, bottomless capacity\, always giving and always "on". Yet
  the wholeness of who we are requires periods of reflection\, receiving an
 d renewal. When we do not honor this necessary balance\, the wisdom of our
  hearts is harder to hear.What's growing in your life? What needs to be no
 urished for further growth? What do you want to prune or clear out?How do 
 we listen to and honor what we need to be whole and in balance amid the de
 mands and desires of an abundant life\, in a way that allows for spaciousn
 ess\, authenticity and joy?How do we tend to the garden of our lives and o
 ur work so that we can receive what we need to flourish?  Held during a ti
 me of peak growth and seasonal abundance\, this Courage to Lead® two-day 
 workshop invites us into spacious time for reflection\, connection\, and i
 nner growth.Together we will…      Pause and cultivate our capacity to b
 e present          Meaningfully engage with ourselves\, others and nature 
 with spaciousness and care          Take stock of our relationship to abun
 dance and consider intentional paths of growth and clearing          Devel
 op skills for holding meaningful conversations and building relational tru
 st          Explore reflective and creative practices including the SoulCo
 llage (https://soulcollage.com/about/)® method\, an expressive arts pract
 ice used as a tool for accessing personal and archetypal wisdom      To en
 sure your SoulCollage (https://soulcollage.com/about/)® materials packet 
 arrives before the workshop\, register by June 24.Details &amp\; Registrat
 ionDates and Times: Thursday-Friday\, July 9-10\, 2026\, 9:30 a.m.-2:30 p.
 m. PT\, OnlineFacilitator: Matsya Siosal\, and&#160\;Rafaela Steen\, LCSWR
 egistration: $225. Includes 9 PDUs or CEUs\, and materials packetRegister 
 Online (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735427?epid=a1aUY000002Wikj)Scholarsh
 ip Fund: We strive to keep our Courage retreats accessible to all who wish
  to participate. Please consider making a tax-deductible donation (https:/
 /engage.lclark.edu/register/gsecgiving?sys:gift:fund=4dfb9f4e-7351-4d84-91
 fe-531631c248c7&amp\;sys:gift:notes=Courage%20and%20Renewal%20Retreats%20S
 cholarship%20Fund) to our scholarship fund.About the Facilitators Matsya S
 iosal has developed her skills in leadership and facilitation for over 25 
 years\, including roles with small and large for-profit corporations\, mis
 sion-driven consumer goods companies\, higher education\, and as a consult
 ant and entrepreneur. She has served as the director of the Center for Com
 munity Engagement at Lewis &amp\; Clark since 2015\, after joining the dep
 artment in 2010 to work in marketing and program management. Matsya is als
 o co-founder and managing partner of Sea-O-Salt Bath Company (http://www.s
 eaosalt.com/). Matsya is an experienced certified facilitator of Courage &
 amp\; Renewal programs. She has facilitated Circle of Trust\, Courage to L
 ead\, and Leading Together workshops and retreats since 2019\, and is trai
 ned as a SoulCollage® (https://soulcollage.com/) facilitator. As a facili
 tator and coach\, Matsya supports mission-driven leaders in accessing thei
 r authentic voice\, and finding clarity and self-trust so they can show up
  with wholeheartedness and sustainability in their lives and work. Rafaela
  Steen\, LCSW has been bringing people together for purpose\, support\, an
 d connection for most of her adult life. For the last two decades\, Rafael
 a has worked as an educational leader and strengths-based licensed clinica
 l social worker offering consultation\, guidance\, and professional develo
 pment related to mental health and well-being in K-12 schools and district
 s. Rafaela is an experienced facilitator\, thought partner\, convener\, an
 d problem solver who sees the importance of meaningful connection and joy 
 within communities. Rafaela intentionally and strategically creates proact
 ive\, welcoming communities of care throughout her life\, both personally 
 and professionally.New workshops and trainings are added to our calendar r
 egularly. For the latest on professional development related to your speci
 fic interests\, sign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net
 /4735441)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260330T225432Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/388399-cultivating-spaci
 ousness-and-abundance-courage-to-lea
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  As leaders we
  are often called to come from a place of perpetual productivity\, bottoml
 ess capacity\, always giving and always "on". Yet the wholeness of who we 
 are requires periods of reflection\, receiving and renewal. When we do not
  honor this necessary balance\, the wisdom of our hearts is harder to hear
 .</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em>What's growing in your life? What n
 eeds to be nourished for further growth? What do you want to prune or clea
 r out?</em></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em>How do we listen to and h
 onor what we need to be whole and in balance amid the demands and desires 
 of an abundant life\, in a way that allows for spaciousness\, authenticity
  and joy?</em></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em>How do we tend to the 
 garden of our lives and our work so that we can receive what we need to fl
 ourish?</em></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Held during a time of peak
  growth and seasonal abundance\, this Courage to Lead® two-day workshop i
 nvites us into spacious time for reflection\, connection\, and inner growt
 h.</p><h4 style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Together we will…</strong><
 /h4><ul><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Pause and cultivate our ca
 pacity to be present    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      M
 eaningfully engage with ourselves\, others and nature with spaciousness an
 d care    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Take stock of o
 ur relationship to abundance and consider intentional paths of growth and 
 clearing    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Develop skill
 s for holding meaningful conversations and building relational trust    </
 p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Explore reflective and crea
 tive practices including the <a href="https://soulcollage.com/about/" targ
 et="_blank" rel="noopener">SoulCollage</a>® method\, an expressive arts p
 ractice used as a tool for accessing personal and archetypal wisdom    </p
 ></li></ul><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  To ensure your <a href="https:/
 /soulcollage.com/about/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SoulCollage</a>® 
 materials packet arrives before the workshop\, register by June 24.</p><hr
  /><h2><strong>Details &amp\; Registration</strong></h2><p style="line-hei
 ght: 1.5\;"><strong>Dates and Times:</strong> Thursday-Friday\, July 9-10\
 , 2026\, 9:30 a.m.-2:30 p.m. PT\, Online</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">
 <strong>Facilitator:</strong> Matsya Siosal\, and&#160\;Rafaela Steen\, LC
 SW</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Registration:</strong> $225. I
 ncludes 9 PDUs or CEUs\, and materials packet</p><p style="line-height: 1.
 5\;"><strong><a class="btn-small-style-1" href="https://lclark.tfaforms.ne
 t/4735427?epid=a1aUY000002Wikj">Register Online</a></strong></p><p class="
 p1" style="font-size: 14px\; line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Scholarship Fund:
 </strong> We strive to keep our Courage retreats accessible to all who wis
 h to participate. Please consider making a <a href="https://engage.lclark.
 edu/register/gsecgiving?sys:gift:fund=4dfb9f4e-7351-4d84-91fe-531631c248c7
 &amp\;sys:gift:notes=Courage%20and%20Renewal%20Retreats%20Scholarship%20Fu
 nd">tax-deductible donation</a> to our scholarship fund.</p><hr /><h2 styl
