X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lewis Clark": "https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/387628-understanding-exploring-and-supporting-perimenopause-"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lewis_clark
X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
SUMMARY:Understanding\, Exploring\, and Supporting Perimenopause and Menop
 ause Experiences in The Therapy Room (In-Person)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260710T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260710T100000
DTSTAMP:20260320T102649Z
UID:20260710T160000Z-387628@www.lclark.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260710T090000
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/91/width/80/height/80/crop/1/
 src_region/6,0,246,240/112728_Auds_Professional_Pic__2.rev.1775664717.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Menopause and perimenopause can magnify emotional and psycholo
 gical distress—often showing up as irritability\, mood shifts\, anxiety\
 , depression\, grief\, self-doubt\, brain fog\, and heightened emotional i
 nsecurity. These experiences can disrupt relationships\, work functioning\
 , and a client's sense of identity and self-efficacy. Many clients report 
 little preparation\, limited validation\, and inconsistent guidance on wha
 t to expect or how to cope.  This skills-based training equips clinicians 
 and helping professionals with practical\, trauma-informed\, and culturall
 y responsive tools to support clients who are navigating menopause-related
  mental health and life-transition stress.  Presenter Audrianna J. Gurr\, 
 LPC\, CADCI\, mental health clinician and author of I'm Still Hot! Survivi
 ng and Thriving in Your Mental Health During Menopause\, will guide partic
 ipants through a framework for identifying common emotional patterns\, nor
 malizing the experience without minimizing it\, and selecting concrete int
 erventions that can be used immediately in session.Following this training
 \, participants will have the ability to:      Identify common emotional a
 nd psychological experiences that may intensify during perimenopause/menop
 ause and differentiate them from other clinical presentations          App
 ly a brief session-ready framework for validating menopause-related distre
 ss while supporting client agency and self-compassion          Use the "Th
 ree Tiers" expectations tool to reduce anxiety-driven over-control and sup
 port realistic planning.&#160\;          Teach assertiveness and boundary-
 setting skills using a "Personal Bill of Rights" lens to strengthen self-a
 dvocacy and relational functioning.          Adapt interventions with atte
 ntion to equity and diversity\, including how gender socialization\, cultu
 re\, and systemic barriers shape help-seeking\, access to care\, and empow
 erment during midlife transitions.    Details &amp\; RegistrationDate and 
 Time: Friday\, July 10\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-12 p.m.Location: Lewis &amp\; Clark
  Graduate SchoolPresenter: Audrianna J. Gurr\, LPC\, CADCICost and Credits
 : $79\, includes 3 CEUs. GSEC Alumni\, Adjuncts\, and Clinical Mental Heal
 th Supervisors save 20%. $40 GSEC Student Rate.Register Online (https://lc
 lark.tfaforms.net/wf1W4MQ?epid=a1aUY000002Unjh)  No-cost registration for 
 GSEC Faculty and Staff are currently full. Contact cce@lclark.edu (mailto:
 cce@lclark.edu) to join the waitlist.Accessibility: We are committed to ma
 king our events accessible to all needs and abilities. When registering\, 
 please let us know your access needs. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or cce@lc
 lark.edu (mailto:cce@lclark.edu)&#160\;with questions.Please note: Discoun
 ted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for current students 
 only and do not include continuing education credit (CEU/PDUs)About the In
 structorAudrianna J. Gurr\, LPC\, CADCI\, MA\, MS\, is a Licensed Professi
 onal Counselor in Portland\, Oregon\, with nearly two decades of experienc
 e in community mental health and private practice. She has provided 15\,00
 0+ therapy sessions and integrates CBT\, DBT\, and other evidence-based ap
 proaches. As she navigates the "perimenopause cusp" herself\, she's passio
 nate about helping clients make sense of mood\, sleep\, cognition\, and id
 entity shifts with compassion and clarity. Audrianna holds an MS in Counse
 ling from Portland State University and an MA in International Relations f
 rom the University of Essex (UK). She is the author of I'm Still Hot! Surv
 iving and Thriving in Menopause. She is also developing additional group s
 upports for people moving through perimenopause and menopause.New workshop
 s and trainings are added to our calendar regularly. For the latest on pro
 fessional development related to your specific interests\, sign up for our
  mailing list! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T161207Z
LOCATION:Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/387628-understanding-exp
 loring-and-supporting-perimenopause-
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Menopause and
  perimenopause can magnify emotional and psychological distress—often sh
 owing up as irritability\, mood shifts\, anxiety\, depression\, grief\, se
 lf-doubt\, brain fog\, and heightened emotional insecurity. These experien
 ces can disrupt relationships\, work functioning\, and a client's sense of
  identity and self-efficacy. Many clients report little preparation\, limi
 ted validation\, and inconsistent guidance on what to expect or how to cop
 e.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  This skills-based training equips cl
 inicians and helping professionals with practical\, trauma-informed\, and 
 culturally responsive tools to support clients who are navigating menopaus
 e-related mental health and life-transition stress.</p><p style="line-heig
 ht: 1.5\;">  Presenter Audrianna J. Gurr\, LPC\, CADCI\, mental health cli
 nician and author of <em>I'm Still Hot! Surviving and Thriving in Your Men
 tal Health During Menopause</em>\, will guide participants through a frame
 work for identifying common emotional patterns\, normalizing the experienc
 e without minimizing it\, and selecting concrete interventions that can be
  used immediately in session.</p><h4 style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Fo
 llowing this training\, participants will have the ability to:</strong></h
 4><ul><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Identify common emotional an
 d psychological experiences that may intensify during perimenopause/menopa
 use and differentiate them from other clinical presentations    </p></li><
 li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Apply a brief session-ready framewo
 rk for validating menopause-related distress while supporting client agenc
 y and self-compassion    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      
 Use the "Three Tiers" expectations tool to reduce anxiety-driven over-cont
 rol and support realistic planning.&#160\;    </p></li><li><p style="line-
 height: 1.5\;">      Teach assertiveness and boundary-setting skills using
  a "Personal Bill of Rights" lens to strengthen self-advocacy and relation
 al functioning.    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Adapt 
 interventions with attention to equity and diversity\, including how gende
 r socialization\, culture\, and systemic barriers shape help-seeking\, acc
 ess to care\, and empowerment during midlife transitions.    </p></li></ul
 ><hr /><h2><strong>Details &amp\; Registration</strong></h2><p style="line
 -height: 1.5\;"><strong>Date and Time:</strong> Friday\, July 10\, 2026\, 
 9 a.m.-12 p.m.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Location:</strong>
  Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><stro
 ng>Presenter:</strong> Audrianna J. Gurr\, LPC\, CADCI</p><p style="line-h
 eight: 1.5\;"><strong>Cost and Credits:</strong> $79\, includes 3 CEUs. GS
 EC Alumni\, Adjuncts\, and Clinical Mental Health Supervisors save 20%. $4
 0 GSEC Student Rate.</p><p><strong><a class="btn-small-style-1 btn-small-s
 tyle-1" href="https://lclark.tfaforms.net/wf1W4MQ?epid=a1aUY000002Unjh">Re
 gister Online</a></strong></p><p>  No-cost registration for GSEC Faculty a
 nd Staff are currently full. Contact <a href="mailto:cce@lclark.edu">cce@l
 clark.edu</a> to join the waitlist.</p><div id="lw_widget_30f0017c" class=
 "lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_blurbs lw_widget_id_7119 lw_wid
 get_accessibility_statement lw_widget_pagination"><ul class="lw_widget_res
 ults lw_widget_results_blurbs"><li class="lw_item_1"><div class="lw_blurbs
 _body"><p class="p1" style="font-size: 15px\; line-height: 1.5\;"><em><str
 ong>Accessibility:</strong> We are committed to making our events accessib
 le to all needs and abilities. When registering\, please let us know your 
 access needs. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or <a href="mailto:cce@lclark.edu
 ">cce@lclark.edu</a>&#160\;with questions.<br/></em></p><p class="p1" styl
 e="font-size: 15px\; line-height: 1.5\;"><em><strong>Please note:</strong>
  Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for current s
 tudents only and <strong>do not</strong> include continuing education cred
 it (CEU/PDUs)</em></p></div></li></ul></div><hr /><h2><strong>About the In
 structor</strong></h2><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Audrianna J. G
 urr\, LPC\, CADCI\, MA\, MS\,</strong> is a Licensed Professional Counselo
 r in Portland\, Oregon\, with nearly two decades of experience in communit
 y mental health and private practice. She has provided 15\,000+ therapy se
 ssions and integrates CBT\, DBT\, and other evidence-based approaches. As 
 she navigates the "perimenopause cusp" herself\, she's passionate about he
 lping clients make sense of mood\, sleep\, cognition\, and identity shifts
  with compassion and clarity. Audrianna holds an MS in Counseling from Por
 tland State University and an MA in International Relations from the Unive
 rsity of Essex (UK). She is the author of <em>I'm Still Hot! Surviving and
  Thriving in Menopause</em>. She is also developing additional group suppo
 rts for people moving through perimenopause and menopause.</p><div id="lw_
 widget_470b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_blurbs l
 w_widget_id_3994 lw_widget_opt_in lw_widget_pagination"><ul class="lw_widg
