 -treats-2/
SUMMARY:World Brotherhood Day with Music and Treats
DESCRIPTION:World Brotherhood Day is an Ananda tradition which began in 198
 3. Every year we begin the holy season by giving our first gift to the wor
 ld - the gift of financial support to strengthen the work of Ananda.\n\n"T
 he First Gift of the Season" is an affirmation of faith and support in the
  mission of Paramhansa Yogananda and Swami Kriyananda to share the truth o
 f world brotherhood across the planet. Donations can be given in any amoun
 t\, however\, the World Brotherhood donation is traditionally the amount o
 f approximately one day's wage. \n\nAs Nayaswami Jyotish says\, the energ
 y of Master is "trying to create one world family\, one nation under God\,
  one universal culture\, where there is no such thing as race or religion 
 or creed or national origin\; where everybody in the world is seen as a br
 other and a sister and we are all there because we are children of God."\n
 \nOur evening celebration will include sharing stories\, readings\, music\
 , a personal blessing\, and sharing delicious international treats and sat
 sang. \n\nWe hope to see you there.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://anandaportland.org/wp-content/uploads/20
 25/02/jesus-holding-the-world.jpg
